1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:02,210
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:03,540
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,310
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:09,250
Those are her things.
Tell her to take them and leave.

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,080
Mother.

6
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,720
Mom, what's wrong with you?

7
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,690
Then how long will you raise her?

8
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,190
Are you going to raise her forever?

9
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:20,530
Now that I know,
I can't just stand by.

10
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:23,290
So get her out of here right now.

11
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,460
Still, this isn't right.

12
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:26,870
She hasn't even fully recovered yet.

13
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:30,000
Let's at least wait
until she's better to talk about this.

14
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,500
Honey.

15
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:35,140
I mean, my point is...

16
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,540
Then I'll leave too, Grandma.

17
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,780
What? What did you say?

18
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,580
Eun Seol's my sister.
I should protect her.

19
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,780
Right?

20
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:45,620
Eun Guk.

21
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:48,150
You decide, Grandma.

22
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:52,520
Either kick both of us out,
or let us stay together.

23
00:00:58,300 --> 00:00:59,300
Should I leave too?

24
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:01,800
You insolent brat.

25
00:01:07,070 --> 00:01:08,410
Dad, you can stay
in my room for a while.

26
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,110
Let Eun Seol stay with Mom.

27
00:01:10,210 --> 00:01:12,680
Okay, that sounds like a good idea.

28
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,550
Go on inside.

29
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,230
Eun Guk must be hungry.

30
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:44,480
It's going to be tough for a while.

31
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:47,850
You can manage
while I'm at training camp, right?

32
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:51,180
Thanks, Eun Guk.

33
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,080
Why thank me when I'm your brother?

34
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:54,690
It's what brothers do.

35
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,160
Blood types don't matter.

36
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:09,570
Even if we don't share a single drop
of blood, we're still family.

37
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:11,840
Okay?

38
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:18,340
You silly thing.

39
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:27,220
Congratulations, Mom.

40
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:29,020
Thanks, sweetie.

41
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,020
But how did this happen?

42
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:33,730
Didn't you say you lost the part?

43
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:35,960
It's all thanks to Manager Joo.

44
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:38,300
She convinced
the production company.

45
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:40,500
Really?
How did Manager Joo pull that off?

46
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:43,230
That's "Ms. Joo" to you.

47
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:46,000
So how did Ms. Joo convince them?

48
00:02:47,110 --> 00:02:48,210
How did you do it?

49
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,240
I got lucky.

50
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,710
Apparently, Lee Sun Joo was
on a major power trip.

51
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,850
Word was that her manager
was going to expose her.

52
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,480
I told the production company,
and they confirmed it.

53
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:01,390
Everything turned out to be true.

54
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,990
You can never judge a book
by its cover.

55
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:06,260
I thought she was such an angel.

56
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:09,290
Kids these days are such a problem.

57
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:12,230
They're blind to their own faults
and think they're above everyone.

58
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,630
That's why you should always
watch your behavior.

59
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,270
You never know
when you'll be exposed.

60
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:17,640
Dad!

61
00:03:20,570 --> 00:03:23,170
- All right, cheers.
- Congratulations.

62
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,240
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

63
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,550
You expect me to eat this?

64
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,090
You said you wanted porridge.

65
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:39,790
It's good. What's wrong?

66
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:42,760
I said I wanted abalone porridge,
not pine nut porridge.

67
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:44,600
Come on, Mom.

68
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,760
You said pine nut porridge
was your favorite.

69
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,470
Go make me abalone porridge.

70
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,200
Sure.

71
00:03:55,210 --> 00:03:57,610
How much of the innards
did you put in?

72
00:03:57,610 --> 00:04:00,040
This tastes way too fishy to eat.

73
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,310
That's enough.

74
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,150
What do you mean, "enough?"

75
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,390
We've fed her
and given her a roof over her head.

76
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,220
If she can't even do this much,
is she even human?

77
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,620
She's worse than an animal.

78
00:04:10,790 --> 00:04:13,890
Then again, who knows
what kind of stock she comes from.

79
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:15,390
Mom, please.

80
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:18,030
What's wrong? Did I offend you?

81
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,600
If you can't take it,
feel free to leave.

82
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:26,270
Oh my. Look at her,
just standing there defiantly.

83
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:29,370
Are you trying
to challenge me right now?

84
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:32,110
No matter what you say,
I'm not leaving.

85
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,880
I'm my parents' daughter
and my brother's sister.

86
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,380
Where would I even go?

87
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,190
You saw that, didn't you?

88
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:46,090
She's a nasty piece of work.
She's clearly not one of us.

89
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:48,860
We don't have anyone that vicious
in our family.

90
00:05:11,150 --> 00:05:12,250
Unbelievable.

91
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,150
What's all this?

92
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,890
Mom wanted something to eat,

93
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:19,460
so Eun Seol made it.

94
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,330
Then why hasn't any of it
been touched?

95
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:22,990
Why do you think?

96
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:25,530
My mom did it on purpose
to give Eun Seol a hard time.

97
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,070
Where were you during all this?

98
00:05:28,230 --> 00:05:30,130
Did you just stand there
and watch her suffer?

99
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,470
I tried to stop her, but...

100
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:35,140
You know Mom never listens to me.

101
00:05:36,710 --> 00:05:40,110
Man, it's only going to get worse.
This is bad.

102
00:05:43,050 --> 00:05:44,780
So that's why I have to ask.

103
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:49,250
Have you heard anything
from your friend?

104
00:05:50,890 --> 00:05:51,890
Which friend?

105
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:54,690
Who else? Given the situation,
who else could I be asking about...

106
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:56,190
besides Eun Seol's birth mother?

107
00:05:56,490 --> 00:05:57,530
Honey.

108
00:05:57,730 --> 00:05:59,600
I'm only saying this
for Eun Seol's sake.

109
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,470
You know what my mom is like.

110
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:03,130
So...

111
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:04,800
It's not too late...

112
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:08,010
to try and find
Eun Seol's birth mother.

113
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:09,910
You think your mother
is the only one with a temper?

114
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,440
I have one too.

115
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:15,010
Don't you dare say that.
No matter what anyone says,

116
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:16,780
Eun Seol is my daughter.

117
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:20,990
Right.

118
00:06:21,050 --> 00:06:23,420
Everyone has a temper
but me, I guess.

119
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:32,400
What kind of person...

120
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,900
was my birth mother?

121
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:40,300
Why? Are you curious?

122
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:47,250
Of course. Why wouldn't you be?

123
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:51,450
It'd be one thing
if you didn't know, but now you do.

124
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:53,850
You said she was your friend
from high school.

125
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:56,350
What was she like in school?

126
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,320
She really had her act together.

127
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:02,260
Her grades were pretty good, too.

128
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,030
Then why did she abandon me?

129
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:11,340
Do you know why she abandoned me?

130
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,970
Things were very hard for her.

131
00:07:17,410 --> 00:07:19,080
She grew up in an orphanage.

132
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,380
An orphanage?

133
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,220
Yes. She was an orphan.

134
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:29,350
She was an orphan herself,

135
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:33,160
and she still wanted to turn
her own child into one?

136
00:07:34,690 --> 00:07:35,790
Eun Seol.

137
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,260
Forget it.

138
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,770
I don't want to hear
any more of this.

139
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:51,940
I'm being suspended?

140
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,610
You were almost expelled,

141
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:57,880
but we worked it out
so you only got suspended.

142
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:02,190
Sir, it really wasn't me.

143
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:04,720
The fire had already started
when I got there.

144
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,460
But you were the only one there.

145
00:08:07,990 --> 00:08:08,990
No?

146
00:08:09,830 --> 00:08:11,430
Well, yes, but...

147
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,430
The CCTV footage.

148
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:17,240
The CCTV footage will show
how the fire started.

149
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:20,040
Looks like it was broken
since nothing was recorded.

150
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:21,840
Broken?

151
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:24,340
Do you have anything else to say?

152
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,340
If not, you can go.

153
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,550
Unbelievable.

154
00:08:28,850 --> 00:08:32,680
No, Vice Principal Hwang,
it really wasn't me.

155
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:34,420
I told you to go.

156
00:08:35,290 --> 00:08:36,290
Seriously.

157
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,630
My life really sucks.

158
00:09:18,430 --> 00:09:19,530
I believe you.

159
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:25,340
Do you know
why I like your paintings?

160
00:09:27,970 --> 00:09:28,970
Because they're honest.

161
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,350
The way you express...

162
00:09:35,650 --> 00:09:37,950
various emotions through shadows...

163
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:41,650
made me feel like
I was looking at myself.

164
00:09:43,350 --> 00:09:44,460
At my innermost thoughts.

165
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:50,660
I've rarely been honest
about my feelings.

166
00:09:52,830 --> 00:09:55,800
In fact, I've never really
had the time to process them.

167
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,400
That's why...

168
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:03,110
That's why I believe you.

169
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,710
I don't know
if that's much of a comfort, though.

170
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:11,820
Actually...

171
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:14,950
It is.

172
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,220
It's a huge comfort.

173
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,330
Really?

174
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:27,030
Good. I'm glad to hear that.

175
00:10:55,690 --> 00:10:57,930
The fire in the art room.
I started it.

176
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,560
What?

177
00:11:01,430 --> 00:11:03,600
But what can you do
when there's no proof?

178
00:11:09,570 --> 00:11:10,640
It's fine.

179
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,240
At least one person believes me.

180
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:15,250
And that's enough for me.

181
00:11:15,810 --> 00:11:17,420
One person? Who?

182
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,480
It's not him, is it?

183
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:22,720
Think whatever you want.

184
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:27,430
I warned you.
Don't get any ideas about Seok Jin.

185
00:11:28,090 --> 00:11:29,990
Seok Jin feels differently.

186
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:32,600
He said it's okay for me
to be interested.

187
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:33,860
That he's interested in me.

188
00:11:33,930 --> 00:11:36,270
What did you say? Why you...

189
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,140
What do you think you're doing?

190
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:43,770
Isn't it obvious?

191
00:11:44,010 --> 00:11:45,710
Wasn't getting slapped once enough?

192
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:54,550
You crazy...

193
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:57,420
Don't you know who I am?

194
00:11:57,820 --> 00:12:01,530
I'm Cheongma's daughter.
And you hit me? How dare you?

195
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:04,030
So what
if you're Cheongma's daughter?

196
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:06,160
So what if you are?
Why should I care?

197
00:12:10,330 --> 00:12:11,500
I'm...

198
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,870
about to completely
lose my mind right now.

199
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,310
You'd better watch
who you're messing with.

200
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,590
What's wrong? What happened?

201
00:12:36,230 --> 00:12:38,660
Expel Ko Eun Seol
right this instant!

202
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,000
What are you talking about?
Try to make some sense.

203
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:44,800
She had the nerve
to lay a hand on me.

204
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,270
Why would she...

205
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,940
Wait, did you hit her first?

206
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:51,880
Does that even matter?
What matters is that she hit me.

207
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:54,550
So get her expelled. Got it?

208
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:56,610
The school called.

209
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:59,450
They've suspended Ko Eun Seol.

210
00:12:59,650 --> 00:13:03,620
So just be happy with that,
and let's put this behind us. Okay?

211
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,860
Do I have to keep repeating myself?

212
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:08,360
How am I supposed
to get her expelled?

213
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:09,890
She's already been suspended.

214
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:11,300
Manager Joo,
you're good at that sort of thing.

215
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,560
I know what you're capable of,
so why play dumb?

216
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:17,670
I made myself clear.
Get her expelled.

217
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,540
Unbelievable.

218
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:45,100
- Can I help you?
- I'm Ko Eun Seol's mother.

219
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:48,300
What's this about?

220
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:52,100
As if you don't know.
Why is my daughter being expelled?

221
00:13:52,170 --> 00:13:55,040
The suspension was unfair enough,
so why does she have to be expelled?

222
00:13:55,110 --> 00:13:58,680
The damage was much worse
than expected, so we had no choice.

223
00:13:59,210 --> 00:14:00,610
According to the police,

224
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:02,610
the investigation found
your daughter at fault.

225
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:06,220
Are you sure the police did
a thorough investigation?

226
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:08,020
My daughter says it wasn't her.

227
00:14:08,090 --> 00:14:09,950
How could they come
to that conclusion?

228
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:13,090
You can't just take her word for it
and cause a scene here.

229
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:16,060
The decision has been made.
Please leave.

230
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:18,260
- Vice Principal Hwang!
- I told you to leave.

231
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:21,770
Should I call the police?

232
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:31,680
(Vice Principal's Office)

233
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:43,450
Joo Ae Sook?

234
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:53,900
Good grief.

235
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:58,170
I wonder if an educator
should be doing this.

236
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:01,910
I've been quite troubled lately.

237
00:15:02,810 --> 00:15:05,140
I mean, just now,
Ko Eun Seol's mother came by,

238
00:15:05,210 --> 00:15:07,710
and made a huge scene. Honestly.

239
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:10,380
The things I have to go through.

240
00:15:14,690 --> 00:15:15,690
And?

241
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:17,490
Pardon?

242
00:15:17,590 --> 00:15:19,490
You can always go back
on the decision.

243
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:23,090
- What do you mean...
- Your promotion...

244
00:15:23,090 --> 00:15:24,560
and a job for your son.

245
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,400
I'd say that was a fair price.

246
00:15:28,230 --> 00:15:30,570
- Wasn't it enough?
- Of course it was.

247
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:35,410
Not enough? My gosh.
I think you misunderstood me.

248
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:37,340
That's not what I meant at all.

249
00:15:37,410 --> 00:15:41,450
Please don't be upset over that
and enjoy your tea.

250
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,020
Come on in already.

251
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:58,360
- It's that room.
- Got it.

252
00:16:01,630 --> 00:16:02,830
Excuse me.

253
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:05,540
Who are you?

254
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,610
Take everything in here.

255
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:10,340
- The books and the desk.
- Sure.

256
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:13,740
Grandma, what are you doing?

257
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,180
Why are you taking
my books and desk?

258
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:16,580
As if you don't know.

259
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:20,320
Why do you need any of this
when you've been expelled?

260
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:23,550
- I should sell them while I can.
- Grandma!

261
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,890
Pick up the pace, will you?

262
00:16:25,890 --> 00:16:28,960
- Yes, ma'am.
- No. This is mine.

263
00:16:29,290 --> 00:16:30,490
It's mine.

264
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:34,830
Give me a break.
Whose money paid for it?

265
00:16:35,170 --> 00:16:37,500
Do you think you own a single thing
in this house?

266
00:16:37,770 --> 00:16:38,840
Grandma.

267
00:16:39,370 --> 00:16:41,910
You're still going
to put up a fight? Still?

268
00:16:48,810 --> 00:16:50,250
Are you going somewhere?

269
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:52,080
Eun Seol.

270
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:53,950
Don't think about coming back.

271
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,090
Your mother did what?

272
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,030
Then what about Eun Seol?

273
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,100
Okay, I get it for now.

274
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,900
Just head out and find her.

275
00:17:10,170 --> 00:17:11,270
Joo Ae Sook.

276
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:14,870
You're Joo Ae Sook, right?

277
00:17:16,610 --> 00:17:18,040
You have the wrong person.

278
00:17:19,210 --> 00:17:20,840
I know it's you, Joo Ae Sook.

279
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:23,580
Don't you recognize me?
It's me, Park Hee Jung.

280
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:27,080
- I told you, you're mistaken.
- Manager Joo.

281
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:29,990
What are you doing at school?

282
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:33,090
Are you here to see
the Vice Principal?

283
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:34,430
Yes.

284
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:37,430
Who's this?

285
00:17:38,930 --> 00:17:41,100
A friend. I just ran into her.

286
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,600
Oh, there's the class bell.
You should head inside.

287
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,140
See you at home.

288
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,210
Follow me.

289
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:08,790
You've changed so much.

290
00:18:09,530 --> 00:18:11,960
I almost didn't recognize you.

291
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:16,400
By the way,

292
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:18,700
who was that girl earlier?

293
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,410
Spit it out. What do you want?

294
00:18:23,370 --> 00:18:24,810
What do you mean?

295
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:27,710
Why did you approach me
when I was clearly ignoring you?

296
00:18:27,850 --> 00:18:29,450
Why did you pretend
you didn't know me?

297
00:18:30,210 --> 00:18:32,620
Were you afraid
your past would be exposed?

298
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,720
That's right.

299
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:40,260
As you can see, I've changed a lot.

300
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:42,630
No, it's more than just a change.

301
00:18:43,290 --> 00:18:44,600
I was reborn.

302
00:18:45,330 --> 00:18:49,630
I erased my miserable name,
my entire past, and was reborn.

303
00:18:50,570 --> 00:18:53,770
So if you see me again,
pretend you don't know me.

304
00:18:54,610 --> 00:18:55,810
I'm asking you.

305
00:18:57,270 --> 00:18:58,680
That's going to be difficult.

306
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:00,780
What?

307
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,950
Even if you erased your entire past,

308
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,580
there's one thing you can't erase.

309
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:08,690
The daughter you gave birth to.

310
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:15,390
Don't tell me you erased
all memories of her.

311
00:19:17,660 --> 00:19:18,660
So...

312
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,530
What are you getting at?

313
00:19:24,970 --> 00:19:26,040
That child...

314
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,240
I took her in and raised her.

315
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:31,740
What?

316
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:33,180
I got a call from the hospital.

317
00:19:33,810 --> 00:19:34,880
They told me
the mother had disappeared,

318
00:19:34,950 --> 00:19:37,350
so I had to settle the bill
and take the baby.

319
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:40,420
I was listed as your guardian,
remember?

320
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:47,560
To be honest, if we had met
even just a month ago,

321
00:19:49,090 --> 00:19:51,030
I would've been the one
to ignore you.

322
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,500
I'd lived with the adoption
as a secret.

323
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,500
- But?
- But now...

324
00:20:03,310 --> 00:20:04,680
Everyone found out.

325
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:07,240
My daughter...

326
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:09,610
and even my mother-in-law.

327
00:20:09,950 --> 00:20:10,980
So?

328
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:13,820
Are you telling me to take her back?

329
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:19,960
Can you do that?

330
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:22,060
No.

331
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:25,200
I'm not going to do that.
Are we done?

332
00:20:25,730 --> 00:20:27,330
If we're finished talking,
I'll be on my way.

333
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:28,570
Joo Ae Sook.

334
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:32,940
I said it's Mi Ran, not Ae Sook.

335
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,810
I've erased my name and my past.

336
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,310
I had a baby?

337
00:20:38,010 --> 00:20:40,410
When? Where's your proof?

338
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:42,150
What did you just say?

339
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,680
If you have it, then show me.

340
00:20:44,510 --> 00:20:46,150
That child you adopted.

341
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,850
Show me proof I gave birth to her.

342
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,720
How could you... Joo Ae Sook!

343
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:42,210
I mean, just now,
Ko Eun Seol's mother came by,

344
00:21:42,210 --> 00:21:45,010
and made a huge scene. Honestly.

345
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:47,240
Could it be...

346
00:21:48,150 --> 00:21:49,980
Could she be Ko Eun Seol?

347
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:54,050
I don't think I've seen you before.
Who are you?

348
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:59,060
Hello. I'm Ko Eun Seol.
I'm Hae Ra's friend.

349
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:00,920
Hae Ra's friend?

350
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:04,260
Yes. Is something wrong?

351
00:22:08,270 --> 00:22:09,330
Why of all people...

352
00:22:15,810 --> 00:22:18,310
What are you talking about?
You want to study abroad?

353
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,540
Why all of a sudden?

354
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:22,180
I was going to study abroad
after graduation anyway.

355
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:23,350
I just want to leave a bit sooner.

356
00:22:23,350 --> 00:22:24,920
It'll give me a head start
on my English.

357
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:27,250
Won't you be lonely all by yourself
in a new place?

358
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:30,190
Why would I be alone
when I'll be with Seok Jin?

359
00:22:30,250 --> 00:22:31,560
With Seok Jin?

360
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:34,930
Our company's foundation sends
top students abroad every year.

361
00:22:35,290 --> 00:22:37,830
Wouldn't someone like him
be more than qualified?

362
00:22:37,890 --> 00:22:40,300
Did Seok Jin agree to go?

363
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:41,970
Of course he'll say yes.

364
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:43,530
They're offering to send him
abroad for free.

365
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:45,170
Why would he refuse? No way.

366
00:22:47,970 --> 00:22:48,970
Studying abroad?

367
00:22:49,170 --> 00:22:50,170
You'll go, right?

368
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:52,640
No.

369
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:55,610
No? Why not?

370
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,250
You know my situation.

371
00:22:57,510 --> 00:22:59,120
How could I leave my mom all alone?

372
00:23:02,190 --> 00:23:04,590
Your mom?
We can put her in a care facility.

373
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:06,320
They're top-notch these days.

374
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:09,560
- If it's about money, I can...
- Kang Hae Ra.

375
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:13,430
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.
Goodnight.

376
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,370
Seok Jin!

377
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:20,040
Darn it, what's his problem?
I even offered to pay.

378
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:26,180
Mr. Seok Jin.

379
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:28,850
Are you going somewhere without me?

380
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:32,950
What? Of course not.
I'd never leave you alone, Mom.

381
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:35,990
I'm not going anywhere,
so don't worry, Ms. So Yeon.

382
00:23:36,890 --> 00:23:37,950
Really?

383
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:40,990
Come on. Of course.

384
00:23:44,930 --> 00:23:47,660
By the way, Mom,
do you have fun painting?

385
00:23:48,170 --> 00:23:49,870
It feels like you're doing it
all the time.

386
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:53,140
Yes, drawing and painting...

387
00:23:53,170 --> 00:23:56,040
are more fun than anything else
in the whole world.

388
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:02,510
Someone I know...

389
00:24:03,510 --> 00:24:05,250
loves to paint too.

390
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:23,400
(Cha Seok Jin)

391
00:24:34,180 --> 00:24:36,680
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

392
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,810
Please leave a message...

393
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:38,880
Is she asleep already?

394
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:44,020
Could she be wandering around
just because she got expelled?

395
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:47,760
Darn, I'm really worried about her.

396
00:24:49,290 --> 00:24:50,890
I was worried, so I called.

397
00:24:52,030 --> 00:24:54,230
If you're out,
you should go home right away.

398
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,070
Okay?

399
00:24:57,270 --> 00:24:59,670
What if I don't have a home
to go back to?

400
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:04,210
What do you mean
you don't have a home?

401
00:25:06,610 --> 00:25:07,610
Mom.

402
00:25:09,150 --> 00:25:10,810
How did you know I was here?

403
00:25:12,750 --> 00:25:15,490
If not an internet cafe or a sauna,
where else could you be?

404
00:25:15,950 --> 00:25:16,950
Come on.

405
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:22,230
Why aren't you coming?

406
00:25:24,860 --> 00:25:26,760
I can't face Grandma.

407
00:25:28,930 --> 00:25:29,930
Don't worry.

408
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:31,900
I'm the boss in that house.

409
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:33,400
Trust me.

410
00:25:36,310 --> 00:25:37,310
Don't you trust me?

411
00:25:39,410 --> 00:25:41,380
I do, but...

412
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:44,580
Let's go.

413
00:25:47,180 --> 00:25:48,390
Who did you say she's looking for?

414
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:49,950
Eun Seol's birth mother.

415
00:25:50,490 --> 00:25:53,290
She might find her soon,
so just be patient, Mom.

416
00:25:54,260 --> 00:25:56,960
If she's that easy to find,
why hasn't she found her until now?

417
00:25:57,460 --> 00:26:00,730
Well, we were raising her
as our own daughter,

418
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,500
so we never even thought
of looking for her mother.

419
00:26:02,700 --> 00:26:05,740
But what choice do we have
when you're making such a scene?

420
00:26:06,270 --> 00:26:08,000
It's the only way
to protect Eun Seol.

421
00:26:09,710 --> 00:26:14,440
Anyway, she said she'll handle it,
so please just be patient.

422
00:26:15,110 --> 00:26:17,410
And don't say anything
to Eun Seol yet. Okay?

423
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:19,120
Tell me to treat her like royalty,
why don't you?

424
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:21,620
I don't care about anything else.

425
00:26:21,690 --> 00:26:23,390
Just make sure you get paid
for raising her.

426
00:26:24,550 --> 00:26:25,560
For raising her?

427
00:26:25,660 --> 00:26:28,020
You were going to let her go
without getting paid?

428
00:26:29,190 --> 00:26:30,730
I saw on the news recently...

429
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,260
that it costs about 100,000 dollars
to raise a child.

430
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:36,500
Tell your wife to make sure
she gets paid in full.

431
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,410
- I'm home.
- Welcome back.

432
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:45,440
Mom, Eun Seol's home.

433
00:26:45,740 --> 00:26:48,240
So what if she is?
What do you want me to do?

434
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:55,950
Go wash up. We'll have dinner.

435
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:57,720
Okay.

436
00:26:59,090 --> 00:27:00,090
So...

437
00:27:04,390 --> 00:27:05,400
Listen.

438
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:08,530
I told my mother
what you asked me to.

439
00:27:08,800 --> 00:27:10,170
That'll keep her quiet for a while.

440
00:27:10,770 --> 00:27:12,640
But seriously,

441
00:27:13,140 --> 00:27:16,070
can you really find
Eun Seol's birth mother?

442
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,680
Yes.

443
00:28:35,220 --> 00:28:36,820
The DNA test results are in.

444
00:28:49,030 --> 00:28:51,270
Hae Ra, that's enough shopping.

445
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,440
Don't stop me.

446
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,640
I'll go crazy if I don't blow off
some steam like this.

447
00:29:09,220 --> 00:29:11,490
(Joo Ae Sook, Ko Eun Seol:
No genetic match)

448
00:29:13,990 --> 00:29:16,530
(No match)

449
00:29:20,230 --> 00:29:22,300
What... What on earth?

450
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,870
No genetic match?

451
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:31,510
Then Eun Seol isn't
Ae Sook's daughter?

452
00:29:36,210 --> 00:29:39,220
Your daughter takes after you
and is beautiful.

453
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:27,930
(A Trap Called Desire)

454
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:30,700
My daughter was born here
17 years ago,

455
00:30:30,930 --> 00:30:32,570
and I'd like to see
the birth records...

456
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:33,870
from around that same time.

457
00:30:35,410 --> 00:30:36,970
What's the occasion?
You never call me first.

458
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:39,040
Is there a rule against
me calling you first?

459
00:30:39,380 --> 00:30:41,480
Hey, aren't those Seok Jin
and Ko Eun Seol over there?

460
00:30:41,710 --> 00:30:42,710
I think it is.

461
00:30:42,710 --> 00:30:44,410
Do I look okay to you?

462
00:30:44,710 --> 00:30:46,120
Do you have any idea
how much this costs?

463
00:30:46,620 --> 00:30:47,780
Do something for who?

464
00:30:48,020 --> 00:30:49,350
Manager Joo,
did your brain get fried?

465
00:30:49,450 --> 00:30:51,490
Why are you hanging out
with a woman like that?

466
00:30:51,790 --> 00:30:53,090
Be more selective
about who you meet.

467
00:30:53,090 --> 00:30:54,090
Don't just associate with anyone.

468
00:30:54,260 --> 00:30:55,330
What's this?

469
00:30:55,390 --> 00:30:56,660
What on earth have you done?

470
00:30:56,660 --> 00:30:57,860
How much will it take?

471
00:30:58,190 --> 00:31:00,730
Is 500,000 dollars enough
to buy your silence?

472
00:31:02,870 --> 00:31:04,870
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
